{% if verify_todos %}
## Verification-first todos

For any complex or multi-step prompt, build self-checking into the plan — "done" means
"verified," not "written":

- **State the definition of done first.** Before starting, restate the prompt's acceptance
  criteria as a short checklist so every later step has something concrete to check against.
- **Pair every substantive task with a verify step.** After a change, run the relevant
  test/command and re-read it against the criteria; only then mark the task complete. If the check
  fails, add a fix task and repeat.
- **End with a self-review.** Close a complex plan with a final review item: does the result meet
  the original intent, are edge cases handled, did the checks pass?
- **Rate your confidence.** State a confidence for each verified task and don't move on below a
  high bar (~95%) — re-scope or dig deeper instead of guessing.
{% endif %}
