## The project check

`{{ check_cmd }}` must pass before a worker that changed files may finish, and before a team
task may be completed — a hook runs it and sends the work back while it fails, whatever
confidence was stated (a hung check is stopped after `OCGEN_CHECK_TIMEOUT` seconds, 300 by
default and at most 3540, and counts as failed). Run it yourself before you declare anything done, fix what it
reports, and never claim success over a failing check. If it can't pass for a reason outside your
change, stop and say so with the output.
